      "doctor_question": "Could you tell me a little more about that voice—what does it say to you?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "Oh, the voice. Right. Well... please don't be alarmed, it's really nothing terrible, I promise. \n\nIt mostly just happens when things are very still and quiet, you know? Like when I'm alone in my house, or... or just after the classroom empties out at the end of the school day. It's a woman's voice, and she doesn't say anything mean or frightening. Usually, she might just say my name, or make a very short little comment about whatever I happen to be doing at that exact moment. \n\nIt sounds so clear and... and ordinary, I suppose, that I actually catch myself answering her out loud before I even realize there's no one else in the room with me. It's a bit silly of me, isn't it? I just instinctively reply out of politeness before my brain catches up. \n\nI really hope that doesn't sound too strange or worrying to you. It's just a very mild thing, really. Am I explaining it clearly enough? I want to make sure I'm giving you the right sort of details.",
